 {
  "schema_set_version": "2.0.0",
  "course_id": "ma-hs10-chemistry",
  "grade": 10,
  "subject": "science",
  "title": "Chemistry",
  "description": "A household-safe laboratory chemistry course covering the full HS-PS1 band from measurement and atomic structure through bonding, reactions, stoichiometry, energy, kinetics, equilibrium, and nuclear change. Because the course is named Chemistry, it satisfies the second statutory credit directly and no department determination of benchmark equivalency is required. No investigation uses concentrated acids or bases, compressed gases, a fume hood, or any chemical needing institutional disposal, and the prohibition on mixing household cleaning products is stated in every unit and cannot be disabled.",
  "capstone": "A chemistry engineering defense: analyse a materials or energy challenge, model a chemical solution with its energy and nuclear trade-offs, evaluate against prioritised criteria, and defend the revisions.",
  "days": 108,
  "order": 2,
