  "grade": 11,
  "subject": "science",
  "title": "Physics",
  "description": "A quantitative laboratory physics course covering forces, momentum, gravitation and electrostatics, energy, thermal physics, fields and induction, waves, and electromagnetic radiation. Placed in Grade 11 so it follows Algebra I and Geometry and runs alongside Algebra II - a Manuel Academy sequencing decision, not a state requirement. All electrical work uses single low-voltage cells; mains electricity and lasers are excluded from the course entirely.",
